Keep the lumped R-L-C extension's state and coefficients in double precision

Applies to thliebig/openEMS 65f8771 (the openEMS submodule of openEMS-Project f73bf97).
Applied by worker/openems-image/Dockerfile; the base image tag carries a hash of it.

The series ADE (LEtype=1) advances J with J0 = ib0 (V0 - V2) - (b1 ib0) J1 - (b2 ib0) J2.
Its characteristic polynomial at z = 1 is 1 + b1 ib0 + b2 ib0 = 4 dT^2 / D, about
(w0 dT)^2: the whole capacitor term. With FDTD_FLOAT (float), b1 ib0 is about -2 and b2 ib0
about 1, each rounded to about 1e-7, so once (w0 dT)^2 is near 1e-7 the capacitor is lost
to rounding. A 100 pF, 0.45 nH part at a 84 fs timestep drained through 50 ohm with
13.3 ns instead of 5 ns; at 481 fs it was right. The R-L form (no C) has the same
cancellation in its z = 1 root. Keeping the extension's own arrays in double removes it;
the field arrays stay float.

